val of 3.8 to 7.2. December accounts for 2% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 3% of all its works contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 39,033.80 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The data shows a pattern of contracts just under the limit, but it doesn't prove any wrongdoing. Prices may be close to the limit due to market conditions or budget constraints. The statistical ratio alone doesn't indicate improper actions by the body or awardees.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see if the amount is unusually close to the limit. Review the contracts of awardee A to see if they frequently win contracts near the limit. Look at the dates and distribution of contracts to identify any unusual patterns or repeated requests for similar services.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"obras","citas":["OftGs8Jy%2BU%2FIGlsa0Wad%2Bw%3D%3D","2ow3ajZx8xDLIx6q1oPaMg%3D%3D","ckrs1ZHGpYd%2FP7lJ7Fu0SA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}